  - label: How we craft
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background: var(--paper);">
            <div class="container">
              <div class="section-head reveal">
                <span class="eyebrow centered">How We Craft Every Journey</span>
                <h2 class="display-h2">Built, re-walked, and guarded — not assembled</h2>
                <p>Great trips aren't pulled from a catalog. Every Jing · Meet China journey is designed by someone who has traveled it, looked after by a real person from start to finish, and held to the standard we'd want for our own family.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="craft-grid">
                <div class="card craft-card reveal">
                  <span class="craft-num">01</span>
                  <h3>Routes we've walked ourselves</h3>
                  <p>Every itinerary is designed by a travel designer who has personally traveled it — and re-scouted at least once a year. No brochure copy, no secondhand routes.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card craft-card reveal reveal-d1">
                  <span class="craft-num">02</span>
                  <h3>One person, from first email to last goodbye</h3>
                  <p>You get a dedicated travel designer who plans your trip and a 24/7 coordinator who stays with you on the ground. No call-center handoffs, no strangers.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card craft-card reveal reveal-d2">
                  <span class="craft-num">03</span>
                  <h3>A guardian on every journey</h3>
                  <p>We treat each trip as if the founder were a guest. If something slips, we fix it before you notice — then we ask, at the end, what we could have done better.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>
